://api.github.com/users/anthonylei/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonylei/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":4604014165,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAAgUXs8AAAABEmuuVQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scrapy/scrapy/labels/spam","name":"spam","color":"6A4C81","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-10-24T07:30:45Z","updated_at":"2026-10-24T07:37:35Z","closed_at":"2026-10-24T07:37:25Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":true,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scrapy/scrapy/pulls/8401","html_url":"https://github.com/scrapy/scrapy/pull/8401","diff_url":"https://github.com/scrapy/scrapy/pull/8401.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/scrapy/scrapy/pull/8401.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Require Brotli >=1.2.1 for [CVE-2026-111497](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-9v8h-qqgm-4m35), following the [upstream security fix](https://github.com/google/brotli/releases/tag/v1.2.1). The previous >=1.2.0 floor already permitted fixed versions on fresh installs, but still allowed vulnerable 1.2.0, which the minimum-dependency and documentation environments pinned.\n\nValidated on macOS arm64: 79 tests from `tests/test_downloadermiddleware_httpcompression.py`, `tests/test_utils_compression.py`, and `tests/test_utils_versions.py` passed on Python 3.14.7 with current dependencies and Python 3.11.15 with minimum dependencies. Also passed: 645 documentation tests, docs build, pre-commit, mypy (529 files), pylint, sdist build/twine check, and wheel build/metadata checks (Brotli >=1.2.1; Python >=3.11). The full runtime/platform matrix was not run locally.\n\nEvidence limits: the docs build resolved multidict 6.9.1 for aiobotocore's <7 constraint despite the unchanged docs pin of 7.1.0; docs-tests used 7.1.0. The docs requirements output changes only the Brotli pin, but no standalone regeneration log was retained.\n\nAI assistance: ZCode generated the patch; Codex independently reviewed the diff and saved validation evidence.\n\n- [x] I have read the [contributing guide](https://docs.scrapy.org/en/master/contributing.html) and [set up pre-commit](https://docs.scrapy.org/en/master/contributing.html#pre-commit).\n","closed_by":{"login":"wRAR","id":241039,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MTAzOQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/241039?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wRAR","html_url":"https://github.com/wRAR","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wRAR/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wRAR/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wRAR/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wRAR/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wRAR/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wRAR/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wRAR/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wRAR/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wRAR/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scrapy/scrapy/issues/8401/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scrapy/scrapy/issues/8401/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scrapy/scrapy/issues/8400","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scrapy/scrapy","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scrapy/scrapy/issues/8400/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scrapy/scrapy/issues/8400/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scrapy/scrapy/issues/8400/events","html_url":"https://github.com/scrapy/scrapy/pull/8400","id":6008148459,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAAgUXs8AAAABKYR--w","number":8400,"title":"Allow custom download schemes in fetch and parse","user":{"login":"ska2704","id":162553727,"node_id":"U_kgDOCbBffw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/162553727?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ska2704","html_url":"https://github.com/ska2704","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ska2704/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ska2704/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ska2704/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ska2704/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ska2704/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ska2704/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ska2704/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ska2704/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ska2704/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":4604014165,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAAgUXs8AAAABEmuuVQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scrapy/scrapy/labels/spam","name":"spam","color":"6A4C81","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-24T01:45:10Z","updated_at":"2026-10-24T01:45:26Z","closed_at":"2026-10-24T01:45:26Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scrapy/scrapy/pulls/8400","html_url":"https://github.com/scrapy/scrapy/pull/8400","diff_url":"https://github.com/scrapy/scrapy/pull/8400.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/scrapy/scrapy/pull/8400.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Let `fetch` and `parse` accept the same URL schemes as `Request`, including download handlers configured by the spider. Invalid URLs still print the command usage and exit with code 2.\n\nCloses #4530. Related to #4603.\n\nValidation: `tox -e py -- tests/test_command_fetch.py tests/test_command_parse.py tests/test_commands.py -q` (153 passed), the minimum-dependency scheme and argument tests (16 passed), `tox -e mypy,pylint,docs,docs-tests -p 4` (all passed, including 645 documentation tests), and `pre-commit run --all-files` (passed). The six new scheme cases fail on unchanged master with usage error 2.\n\n- [x] I have read the [contributing guide](https://docs.scrapy.org/en/master/contributing.html) and [set up pre-commit](https://docs.scrapy.org/en/master/contributing.html#pre-commit).\n","closed_by":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scrapy/scrapy/issues/8400/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scrapy/scrapy/issues/8400/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scrapy/scrapy/issues/8399","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scrapy/scrapy","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scrapy/scrapy/issues/8399/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scrapy/scrapy/issues/8399/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scrapy/scrapy/issues/8399/events","html_url":"https://github.com/scrapy/scrapy/pull/8399","id":6000408171,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAAgUXs8AAAABKSClng","number":8399,"title":"Parse quoted-string Cache-Control directive values","user":{"login":"guocn","id":11581622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNTgxNjIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11581622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guocn","html_url":"https://github.com/guocn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guocn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guocn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guocn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guocn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guocn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guocn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guocn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guocn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guocn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":4604014165,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAAgUXs8AAAABEmuuVQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scrapy/scrapy/labels/spam","name":"spam","color":"6A4C81","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-23T15:14:18Z","updated_at":"2026-10-23T15:14:33Z","closed_at":"2026-10-23T15:14:33Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scrapy/scrapy/pulls/8399","html_url":"https://github.com/scrapy/scrapy/pull/8399","diff_url":"https://github.com/scrapy/scrapy/pull/8399.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/scrapy/scrapy/pull/8399.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"- [x] I have read the [contributing guide](https://docs.scrapy.org/en/master/contributing.html) and [set up pre-commit](https://docs.scrapy.org/en/master/contributing.html#pre-commit).\n\n`parse_cachecontrol()` split the `Cache-Control` header on every comma, so a directive whose value is a quoted-string containing a comma was broken into bogus directives:\n\n```pycon\n>>> parse_cachecontrol(b'private=\"Set-Cookie, Cookie\", max-age=60')\n{b'private': b'\"Set-Cookie', b'cookie\"': None, b'max-age': b'60'}\n```\n\nQuoted values also kept their quotes, so a valid quoted `max-age=\"60\"` (RFC 9111 §5.2 requires accepting both token and quoted-string forms) failed the `int()` conversion in `_get_max_age()` and was treated as absent — a response served with a quoted `max-age` was therefore never considered fresh by `RFC2616Policy` and got refetched instead of served from cache.\n\nDirectives are now split only on the commas outside quoted-strings, and well-formed quoted values have their quotes and backslash quoted-pair escapes removed, as defined in RFC 9110 §5.6.4. Plain-token and absent values behave exactly as before.\n\nTests: parametrized `test_parse_cachecontrol` cases for quoted values, quoted commas and quoted-pair escapes, plus a `max-age=\"86405\"` sample in the RFC2616 `test_cached_and_fresh` policy test. Full `tests/test_downloadermiddleware_httpcache.py` (158 tests), module doctests, ruff, mypy 2.4.0 and pylint all pass locally.\n\nDrafted with the ZCode agent (claude-fable-5-1) under the direction of @g